Original commit body from 840c98220873b44bc32162f6894bb5d214d5c07d:

deduplicate_edges keeps one edge per (src, dst, edge_type) and unioned only
`line` into `call_lines`. Every other site-varying key on the survivor was the
FIRST edge's value, presented with nothing to mark it partial — so the map did
not merely under-report, it reported a DIFFERENT SITE'S FACT as the
relationship's.

The case that makes it urgent is a real filesystem write disappearing.
Measured end to end on the shipped CLI with a control in the same run:

    def truncate_logs(p):          def truncate_logs(p):
        fh = open(p, 'r')              open(p, 'w').close()
        fh.close()
        open(p, 'w').close()

    io-boundaries: fs_read         io-boundaries: fs_write

Same truncating write. Adding a READ above it deleted fs_write from the
boundary map outright, because the two builtins.open sites collapsed to one
edge carrying io_mode='r' and the mode gate then eliminated the fs_write row.
A `must_not_exist: fs_write` claim confirms on the left — the INV-nufob /
ADR-0033 false-confirm class, reached through the edge collapse rather than
through a catalogue hole, live in Python.

Two more per-site erasures close with it: bash `redirect_target` reported
`echo a > /dev/null` then `echo "$API_KEY" > /etc/cron.d/pwned` as a write to
/dev/null, and `env_var` reported `$HOME` then `$API_KEY` as HOME.

THE RULE IS A GENERALIZATION, NOT AN INVENTION. call_arg_shape has carried
exactly this discipline since INV-fubag — a proof asserted from one site
silences real flows at another — hardcoded for that one key. What was missing
was a way to declare a second, so MetaKeySpec gains `per_call_site` and ir.py
reads the list from the registry rather than owning a copy.

Contract mirrors call_lines: the singular key survives only while every
collapsed site agrees; on disagreement it is REMOVED and the distinct values
move to <key>_values. A site that OMITS the key is itself a disagreement.

Both fs boundaries are reported when the sites span both, rather than trading
the lost write for a lost read: resolve_mode_boundary_across_sites picks
fs_write if ANY site writes (the reverse of the absence direction, and
deliberately — disagreeing sites are evidence, not ignorance), and
mode_spanned_boundaries stamps the plural io_boundaries INV-zumin already
minted for several-facts-one-call. Uniform edges gain no key.

Both collapse sites (deduplicate_edges and apply_external_id_remap) route
through the same function so the rule cannot hold at one and not the other.

